#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""llm-local: ask the LOCAL LLM (llama.cpp llama-server on 127.0.0.1:8179). Never calls a remote API.

  echo "prompt" | llm-local [--system TEXT] [--max-tokens N] [--json] [--temp T] [--stats]
  llm-local --anonymize [--strict] [--owner-name NAME] [--summary] [--stats] < private.txt

Default mode: stdin is the user prompt, the answer goes to stdout. --json asks for a JSON object
(grammar-constrained) and prints it validated, on one line.

--anonymize: stdin text -> stdout with the
same lines, order and wording. KEPT verbatim: names (no aliases), street addresses, places, venues and the facts
(topics, plans, meetings, trips, events, decisions, dates, times, who said what; small everyday shared costs and
bill due dates). REDACTED: intimate or personal passages that don't belong in front of a third-party AI assistant ->
"[private: health | mental health | sexual | dating | relationship | family | money | business | confidential |
gossip]" (the sentence or message part; the rest of the message stays). money = anyone's finances, the owner's
included: salary, savings, investments, portfolio and trading plans, amounts held/invested/earned/owed, debts, bank
details, purchases and their sums, negotiated prices; business = deals, a company or side business, clients,
revenue. MASKED: identifiers -> [phone], [email], [IBAN], [account number], [card number], [AHV number], [ID number],
[secret] (passwords, PINs, codes), [license plate], [birthdate], [link: domain], @[user]; a surname only when its
person is attached to a redacted passage -> [surname]. The owner (--owner-name) -> "You".
The model only DETECTS (grammar-constrained JSON, chunk by chunk): it quotes private sentences with a category and
identifiers with a type. The replacement is done here in code on the original text: quotes are found exactly, then
case/space/punctuation-blind, then by anchor words, then by the best-matching line, and widened to whole sentences;
chat prefixes ("[ts] Name: ") and tgread line tails stay. A regex safety pass then catches phones, emails, IBANs,
account, card and AHV numbers, Swiss plates, birthdates next to "geboren/born", passwords/PINs/codes after a
keyword and token links the model missed, and money amounts -> [amount]: any currency amount from 5'000 up, and
every amount on the same line near a money/business/payment word (Lohn, salary, invest, ETF, Tranche, Deal, Umsatz,
paid, bezahlt, TWINT, receipt, ...) or right after an amount label ("Total:", "Betrag", "amount due").
--all-amounts: the owner's own mail: every currency amount of any size, every labelled number and bare cents
that can't be a time -> [amount] (the vault sets it for Gmail search, get and events).
--keep-own-money: admin documents (the owner's own bills, payslips, tax papers in paperless): only debts and money
troubles are private, no business category, no [amount] net.
--strict: maximum anonymity on top of the private-passage redaction: a second, strict detector also runs
(about twice the detection time), private people -> "Person A/B/..." (consistent across chunks), home addresses ->
[address], home/work locations -> [location].
--summary: anonymize (with --strict if given), then write a detailed summary of the anonymized text (the model never
sees the removed data in that step); --system adds instructions to that summary.
--paraphrase (summarize and paraphrase every message without changing any meaning,
numbers or facts; all remaining redactions still apply): after the anonymization, every message body (chat lines
between '[ts] Name: ' and the ref tail; mail subjects and paragraphs) becomes a short, neutral paraphrase IN ITS OWN LANGUAGE that
keeps every fact, name, place, date, time and number, in one call per batch. No
translation: the paraphrase keeps the item's language and dialect (Swiss German stays Swiss German,
Standard German stays Standard German). Checked in code per message: numbers,
weekdays, months and today/tomorrow/yesterday must occur in its anonymized text, the [placeholders] must be the same,
a clock time stays a time and a date stays a date (Swiss "am 4i" never becomes "the 4th"), a negated sentence keeps a
negation, and the language stays;
one retry, then the anonymized text marked "[not paraphrased]". Headers, refs, senders and times stay as they are; the
regex and money nets run again. With --summary: each summary line is checked the same way (one retry, then left out).

The server is started on demand (llm-server-ctl start) unless --no-start. Exit codes: 0 ok, 2 usage,
3 local LLM unavailable, 4 bad response / request rejected (e.g. too long), 5 timeout.
Backend: "vault" in ~/.config/llm-local/backend (or env LLM_LOCAL_BACKEND=vault) runs everything through the privacy
vault instead (`vault llm-run -- ARGS`: the same llm-local and model inside container claude-vault); "local" or no
file = this box's llama-server.
Env (tests): LLM_LOCAL_PORT, LLM_LOCAL_CTL, LLM_LOCAL_BACKEND, LLM_LOCAL_VAULT_BIN. LLM_LOCAL_STATS_FILE (the vault): one
JSON line of numbers per run (tokens processed/reused, seconds, cache hits), for its health metrics. LLM_LOCAL_TICKET (the
vault): sent as X-LLM-Ticket; the vault's LLM proxy gates each model request with it.
"""
import argparse
import base64
import bisect
import hashlib
import hmac
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.request

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True

PORT = int(os.environ.get("LLM_LOCAL_PORT", "8179"))
BASE = "http://127.0.0.1:%d" % PORT          # loopback only, by construction
CTL = os.environ.get("LLM_LOCAL_CTL", os.path.expanduser("~/bin/llm-server-ctl"))
# The privacy vault's per-request LLM gate: its proxy admits a request only with the ticket of an open LLM job.
TICKET = os.environ.get("LLM_LOCAL_TICKET", "")
# No proxies: an http_proxy in the environment must never route private text off the box.
OPENER = urllib.request.build_opener(urllib.request.ProxyHandler({}))
STATS = []


class LLMError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, msg, code=4):
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.code = code


def die(msg, code):
    print("llm-local: " + msg, file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- server access
def http(path, body=None, timeout=10):
    data = None if body is None else json.dumps(body).encode()
    headers = {"Content-Type": "application/json"}
    if TICKET:
        headers["X-LLM-Ticket"] = TICKET
    req = urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, data=data, headers=headers)
    try:
        with OPENER.open(req, timeout=timeout) as r:
            return json.load(r)
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            detail = json.load(e).get("error", {})
            detail = detail.get("message", detail) if isinstance(detail, dict) else detail
        except Exception:
            detail = e.reason
        raise LLMError("server rejected the request (HTTP %d): %s" % (e.code, detail), 4)
    except TimeoutError:
        raise LLMError("timed out after %ds" % timeout, 5)
    except (urllib.error.URLError, ConnectionError, OSError) as e:
        reason = getattr(e, "reason", e)
        if isinstance(reason, TimeoutError) or "timed out" in str(reason):
            raise LLMError("timed out after %ds" % timeout, 5)
        raise LLMError("cannot reach the local LLM at %s (%s)" % (BASE, reason), 3)


def healthy():
    try:
        return http("/health", timeout=3).get("status") == "ok"
    except LLMError:
        return False


def ensure_server(no_start):
    if healthy():
        return
    if no_start:
        raise LLMError("local LLM server is not running (start it: llm-server-ctl start)", 3)
    # stderr to a temp file, not a pipe: a server child that inherits a pipe would block us until it exits
    with tempfile.TemporaryFile(mode="w+") as err:
        try:
            p = subprocess.run([CTL, "start"], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=err,
                               timeout=300)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            raise LLMError("could not start the local LLM server: %s" % e, 3)
        err.seek(0)
        msg = err.read().strip().splitlines()
    if p.returncode != 0 or not healthy():
        raise LLMError("local LLM unavailable: %s" % (msg[-1] if msg else "llm-server-ctl start failed"), 3)


def chat(messages, max_tokens=1024, temperature=0.7, schema=None, json_mode=False, timeout=1800,
         presence=0.0, label="chat"):
    body = {"messages": messages, "max_tokens": max_tokens, "temperature": temperature,
            "top_p": 0.8, "top_k": 20, "min_p": 0.0, "presence_penalty": presence,
            "cache_prompt": True, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": False}}
    if schema is not None:
        body["response_format"] = {"type": "json_schema", "json_schema": {"name": "out", "schema": schema}}
    elif json_mode:
        body["response_format"] = {"type": "json_object"}
    t = time.time()
    r = http("/v1/chat/completions", body, timeout=timeout)
    try:
        ch = r["choices"][0]
        txt = ch["message"]["content"] or ""
    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError):
        raise LLMError("unexpected response from the local LLM", 4)
    txt = re.sub(r"(?s)^\s*<think>.*?</think>\s*", "", txt).strip()
    tm = r.get("timings") or {}
    STATS.append({"step": label, "wall_s": round(time.time() - t, 1), "prompt_tokens": tm.get("prompt_n"),
                  "cached_tokens": tm.get("cache_n"),
                  "prompt_tps": round(tm.get("prompt_per_second") or 0, 1), "gen_tokens": tm.get("predicted_n"),
                  "gen_tps": round(tm.get("predicted_per_second") or 0, 2),
                  "prompt_s": round((tm.get("prompt_ms") or 0) / 1000, 2),
                  "gen_s": round((tm.get("predicted_ms") or 0) / 1000, 2),
                  "finish": ch.get("finish_reason")})
    return txt, ch.get("finish_reason")


def write_stats_line(path):
    """One JSON line of numbers per run for the privacy vault's health metrics (env LLM_LOCAL_STATS_FILE): model
    calls, prompt tokens processed vs reused from the server's prompt cache, generated tokens, prompt and generation
    seconds, cache hits/misses. Never any text."""
    def tot(k):
        return sum(x.get(k) or 0 for x in STATS if isinstance(x.get(k), (int, float)))
    d = {"ts": int(time.time()), "calls": len(STATS), "prompt_tokens": tot("prompt_tokens"),
         "cached_tokens": tot("cached_tokens"), "gen_tokens": tot("gen_tokens"),
         "prompt_s": round(tot("prompt_s"), 2), "gen_s": round(tot("gen_s"), 2)}
    if CACHE_STATS:
        d["cache"] = {k: list(v) for k, v in CACHE_STATS.items()}
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_APPEND, 0o600)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "a", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(d) + "\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


CACHE_STATS = {}                                 # cache name -> [hits, misses] of this run


def count_tokens(text):
    try:
        return len(http("/tokenize", {"content": text}, timeout=120).get("tokens", []))
    except LLMError:
        return len(text) // 3


def ctx_size():
    try:
        p = http("/props", timeout=5)
        return int(p.get("default_generation_settings", {}).get("n_ctx") or p.get("n_ctx") or 32768)
    except (LLMError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return 32768


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- anonymization cache
# --cache-dir DIR (or env LLM_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR; only with --anonymize/--summary): the privacy vault sets it for its own
# private jobs, never for the caller's own text. Cached: the model's detection result per chunk, its check verdict per
# sentence, and summaries. Keys: HMAC-SHA256 (key DIR/key, 0600) of the policy, the model, the cache kind and the full
# request (system prompt, schema, user message, settings), so a policy, prompt or model change never hits an old
# entry. Detections are stored as positions in the request text plus their enum categories/types, never as text; a
# quote the model didn't copy verbatim is stored encrypted (HMAC-SHA256 keystream under the cache key, per entry and
# string). Checks keep only the verdict; summaries and policy v4 paraphrase batches (built from anonymized text) their
# answer, encrypted the same way. Every code step (locating and widening passages, the surname rule, the regex and money nets)
# still runs on every call, so the output is the same as a fresh run. A corrupt entry is a miss: the work runs again,
# never a fallback to raw text. CACHE_DAYS expiry, CACHE_MAX_BYTES size cap (oldest first).
CACHE_DAYS = 30
CACHE_MAX_BYTES = 200 * 1024 * 1024
CACHE = None
CACHE_KEYS = {"private", "identifiers", "text", "category", "about", "type", "people", "name", "variants", "pii"}
CACHE_ENUMS = {"category", "type"}


class NotCacheable(Exception):
    pass


def to_refs(obj, src, key=None, enc=None, ctr=None):
    """Model output -> the same structure with every string as [position, length] in src (enums kept; a string not
    in src encrypted with enc(n, bytes))."""
    ctr = [0] if ctr is None else ctr
    if isinstance(obj, dict):
        if not all(k in CACHE_KEYS for k in obj):
            raise NotCacheable()
        return {k: to_refs(v, src, k, enc, ctr) for k, v in obj.items()}
    if isinstance(obj, list):
        return [to_refs(x, src, key, enc, ctr) for x in obj]
    if isinstance(obj, str):
        if key in CACHE_ENUMS and re.fullmatch(r"[a-z_]{1,24}", obj):
            return {"e": obj}
        if obj == "":
            return {"@": [0, 0]}
        i = src.find(obj)
        if i >= 0:
            return {"@": [i, len(obj)]}
        if enc is None:
            raise NotCacheable()
        ctr[0] += 1
        return {"x": base64.b64encode(enc(ctr[0], obj.encode("utf-8"))).decode("ascii")}
    if obj is None or isinstance(obj, (bool, int, float)):
        return obj
    raise NotCacheable()


def from_refs(obj, src, enc=None, ctr=None):
    ctr = [0] if ctr is None else ctr
    if isinstance(obj, dict):
        if set(obj) == {"@"}:
            i, n = obj["@"]
            if not (isinstance(i, int) and isinstance(n, int) and 0 <= i and i + n <= len(src)):
                raise ValueError("bad position")
            return src[i:i + n]
        if set(obj) == {"e"}:
            return str(obj["e"])
        if set(obj) == {"x"}:
            if enc is None:
                raise ValueError("no key")
            ctr[0] += 1
            return enc(ctr[0], base64.b64decode(obj["x"])).decode("utf-8")
        if not all(k in CACHE_KEYS for k in obj):
            raise ValueError("bad key")
        return {k: from_refs(v, src, enc, ctr) for k, v in obj.items()}
    if isinstance(obj, list):
        return [from_refs(x, src, enc, ctr) for x in obj]
    return obj


class AnonCache:
    def __init__(self, d):
        self.dir = d
        os.makedirs(d, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        os.chmod(d, 0o700)
        kp = os.path.join(d, "key")
        try:
            with open(kp, "rb") as f:
                self.key = f.read()
            if len(self.key) < 32:
                raise OSError("short key")
        except OSError:
            self.key = os.urandom(32)
            tmp = "%s.%d.tmp" % (kp, os.getpid())
            fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
            with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as f:
                f.write(self.key)
            os.replace(tmp, kp)
        try:
            self.model = os.path.basename(str(http("/props", timeout=10).get("model_path") or "unknown"))
        except (LLMError, AttributeError):
            self.model = "unknown"

    def crypt(self, entry):
        """XOR with an HMAC-SHA256 keystream per (entry, string number): encrypts and decrypts."""
        ek = hmac.new(self.key, b"llm-local cache encryption", hashlib.sha256).digest()

        def f(n, data):
            out, blk = bytearray(), 0
            while len(out) < len(data):
                out += hmac.new(ek, ("%s/%d/%d" % (entry, n, blk)).encode(), hashlib.sha256).digest()
                blk += 1
            return bytes(a ^ b for a, b in zip(data, out))
        return f

    def seal(self, k, text):
        """Text built from anonymized text (summaries, paraphrases) -> an encrypted entry (keystream number 0)."""
        return {"x": base64.b64encode(self.crypt(k)(0, text.encode("utf-8"))).decode("ascii")}

    def unseal(self, k, data):
        """seal()'s entry -> the text, or None (a miss) if it is missing or unreadable."""
        try:
            if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get("x"), str):
                return self.crypt(k)(0, base64.b64decode(data["x"], validate=True)).decode("utf-8")
        except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            pass
        return None

    def key_for(self, kind, req):
        blob = json.dumps([POLICY, self.model, kind, req], sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)
        return hmac.new(self.key, blob.encode("utf-8"), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()

    def path(self, kind, k):
        return os.path.join(self.dir, kind, k[:2], k + ".json")

    def get(self, kind, k):
        p = self.path(kind, k)
        try:
            if time.time() - os.stat(p).st_mtime > CACHE_DAYS * 86400:
                os.unlink(p)
                raise OSError("expired")
            with open(p, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                d = json.load(f)
            if not (isinstance(d, dict) and d.get("v") == 1 and "data" in d):
                raise ValueError("bad entry")
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            CACHE_STATS.setdefault(kind, [0, 0])[1] += 1
            return None
        CACHE_STATS.setdefault(kind, [0, 0])[0] += 1
        return d["data"]

    def put(self, kind, k, data):
        p = self.path(kind, k)
        try:
            for sub in (os.path.join(self.dir, kind), os.path.dirname(p)):    # each level 0700 (makedirs' mode
                try:                                                          # covers only the last one)
                    os.mkdir(sub, 0o700)
                except FileExistsError:
                    pass
            tmp = "%s.%d.tmp" % (p, os.getpid())
            fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
            with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
                json.dump({"v": 1, "data": data}, f, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":"))
            os.replace(tmp, p)
        except OSError:
            pass

    def prune(self):
        """At most once an hour: drop expired entries, then the oldest until the cache is under CACHE_MAX_BYTES."""
        mark = os.path.join(self.dir, ".pruned")
        try:
            if time.time() - os.stat(mark).st_mtime < 3600:
                return
        except OSError:
            pass
        files, total, now = [], 0, time.time()
        for root, _dirs, names in os.walk(self.dir):
            for n in names:
                if n.endswith(".json"):
                    fp = os.path.join(root, n)
                    try:
                        st = os.stat(fp)
                    except OSError:
                        continue
                    if now - st.st_mtime > CACHE_DAYS * 86400:
                        try:
                            os.unlink(fp)
                        except OSError:
                            pass
                        continue
                    files.append((st.st_mtime, st.st_size, fp))
                    total += st.st_size
        for _mt, size, fp in sorted(files):
            if total <= CACHE_MAX_BYTES:
                break
            try:
                os.unlink(fp)
                total -= size
            except OSError:
                pass
        try:
            os.close(os.open(mark, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600))
            os.utime(mark)
        except OSError:
            pass


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- anonymization
# Policy v3: first names, addresses, places and the non-financial facts stay
# verbatim; intimate or personal passages, and anyone's money or business details (the owner's own included), are
# replaced by "[private: <category>]"; identifiers are masked; a surname is masked only when its person is attached
# to a redacted passage. --strict: the old policy (all names aliased, addresses/locations masked) plus the
# private-passage redaction. --keep-own-money (the owner's admin documents): the v2 money rule, no business category.
POLICY = "llm-local-v4.1+regex-2026-10-13"
PRIVATE_CATEGORIES = ["health", "mental_health", "sexual", "dating", "relationship", "family", "money", "business",
                      "confidential", "gossip"]
ADMIN_CATEGORIES = [c for c in PRIVATE_CATEGORIES if c != "business"]
_MONEY_V3 = ("money: money and finances of anyone, the owner included: salary, income, bonus, savings, wealth, account "
             "balances, investments, portfolio, stocks, ETFs, crypto, trades and investment plans, amounts someone holds, "
             "invests, earns, lends, borrows or owes, debts, money problems, debt collection, bank details, purchases and "
             "what they cost (beyond small everyday costs), prices someone negotiates, taxes someone pays")
_BUSINESS_V3 = ("business: business deals, contracts and negotiations, a company, side business or self-employment, "
                "clients, revenue, profit, offers and quotes, bulk purchases and resale")
_MONEY_V2 = "money: someone's debts, money problems, debt collection, being unable to pay rent or bills"
_KEEP_V3 = ("plans, meetings, dates, times, places, venues, travel and trips, events, bills and their due dates, "
            "splitting small everyday costs (pizza, drinks, tickets, a gift collection) and the small amounts friends "
            "owe each other for them, presents")
_KEEP_V2 = ("plans, meetings, dates, times, places, venues, travel, prices, splitting costs, small amounts friends owe "
            "each other (pizza, tickets, gifts), presents")
_PRIVATE_RULES = """"private": every sentence that reveals intimate or very personal matters that do not belong in front of an outside AI assistant, about the writer or about someone else:
- health: illness, diagnosis, injury, symptoms, medication, treatment, surgery, pregnancy, medical test results
- mental_health: depression, anxiety, panic attacks, burnout, therapy, psychiatrist, self-harm, addiction
- sexual: sex, sexual orientation, intimate or body details
- dating: dates, crushes, hookups, dating apps, who is seeing or sleeping with whom
- relationship: breakups, cheating, a couple's fights, divorce, jealousy
- family: conflicts within a family, family members' private problems
- %(money)s%(business)s
- confidential: a personal secret told in confidence ("don't tell anyone", "unter üs")
- gossip: crude or mean personal gossip about someone (looks, drinking, sex life, private life)
For each: "text" = the whole sentence copied EXACTLY as written (a verbatim substring), "category" = one of the categories above, "about" = the name of the person it is about, exactly as written, or "" if it is about the writer.
NOT private, never list: %(keep)s, surprise parties and other surprises, work and school logistics, exams, looking for a doctor or dentist, appointments without medical details, sports, weather, food, jokes, being tired or hungover, everyday moods (happy, stressed, annoyed). Most messages are not private."""
PRIVATE_RULES = _PRIVATE_RULES % {"money": _MONEY_V3, "business": "\n- " + _BUSINESS_V3, "keep": _KEEP_V3}
PRIVATE_RULES_ADMIN = _PRIVATE_RULES % {"money": _MONEY_V2, "business": "", "keep": _KEEP_V2}

DETECT_SYSTEM = """You check text before it is shown to an outside AI assistant. The text can be German, Swiss German or English: chat logs, emails, notes, documents. Names, street addresses, places and normal facts are fine and must NOT be listed. Answer with JSON only.

""" + PRIVATE_RULES + """

"identifiers": every item of these kinds, "text" copied EXACTLY as it appears (a verbatim substring), with a "type":
- phone: phone numbers
- email: email addresses
