- card: credit/debit card numbers
- ahv: AHV/AVS/social security numbers
- id: passport, ID card, customer, insurance policy, tax or other personal ID numbers
- secret: passwords, PINs, door codes, one-time or login codes
- link: links with tokens, share IDs, invite codes or personal IDs
- plate: vehicle license plates
- birthdate: a date of birth with year (e.g. "18.10.1996")
Do NOT list as identifiers: names, street addresses, cities, venues, dates and times of events, amounts and prices, shop order numbers."""

DETECT_SYSTEM_ADMIN = DETECT_SYSTEM.replace(PRIVATE_RULES, PRIVATE_RULES_ADMIN)

# --strict: the pre-v2 detector (people + personal data), unchanged; it runs next to DETECT_SYSTEM, which supplies the
# private passages (one combined prompt made the 9B model skip some of them).
DETECT_SYSTEM_STRICT = """You find personal data in text so that it can be removed. The text can be German, Swiss German or English: chat logs, emails, notes, documents. Answer with JSON only.

"people": every PRIVATE individual who writes or is mentioned: first names, full names, surnames with a title (e.g. "Herr Huber", "Dr. Frei"), nicknames, @usernames. For each person: "name" = the most complete form seen, "variants" = every other form of that person's name that appears in the text, copied exactly as written. If a person is already in the known-people list, use exactly that "name". Do NOT list well-known public figures (celebrities, athletes, artists, DJs, politicians), companies, shops, bars, restaurants, venues, brands, streets or places, and not relationship words alone (Mama, Chef, boss).

"pii": every other item of personal data, each "text" copied EXACTLY as it appears (a verbatim substring), with a "type":
- phone: phone numbers
